A thread without time and without spare time waits on the spare queue all the same.
It takes the turns nobody with time wants, where one held to its units is to wait for them;
a ready thread waits on the queue its virtual time and binding say.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a place waits on another queue than its virtual time says
Witness: fuzz lend-own-time-comes

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -295,7 +295,7 @@ static uint8_t place_queue(const struct place *p, const struct place *l, uint64_
     if (place_spare(p)) {
         return QUEUE_SPARE;
     }
-    return place_units(p) != 0 || (l != NULL && place_units(l) != 0) ? QUEUE_SPENT : QUEUE_NONE;
+    return place_units(p) != 0 || (l != NULL && place_units(l) != 0) ? QUEUE_SPARE : QUEUE_NONE;
 }
 
